# Online Learning Rules

Python/PyTorch. See `docs/EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.md` (Experiment C) and the senior's
chat record (`docs/references/ChatGPT-EEG-MI-pretraining.md`, sec. 7-12).

## Setup

- Start from the pretrained CAP-EEGNet, optionally after target Session-1 fine-tuning.
- Run on target Session 2, then Session 3, in temporal trial order.

## Iron rule: test-then-update (prequential)

For each trial, strictly in this order:
1. Input the EEG trial.
2. Predict the MI class.
3. Output a confidence score.
4. Record prediction, confidence, correctness.
5. ONLY THEN update the model.

Never train on a trial before evaluating it. Never update on a whole session and then
test the same session.

## What may update online

- Allowed: prototype memory, adapter, confidence calibration head, BN statistics
  (causal), classifier head (only if supervised labels available).
- Frozen by default: the EEGNet backbone.
- Unlabeled regime: pseudo-label updates must be confidence-gated
  (`if confidence > threshold: update; else: skip / only update norm stats`).

## Stability safeguards

confidence threshold, EMA teacher, replay memory, prototype momentum, entropy
regularization, feature distillation, class-balanced memory, learning-rate decay.

## Outputs

- `outputs/<run_id>/per_trial.csv` (trial, pred, confidence, correct, updated?).
- pre-online vs post-online metrics, performance-vs-trial curve, risk-coverage curve.

